# Built binaries, anchored to the repo root. Without the leading slash this
# would also match the SOURCE directory cmd/tool-store/, so a new .go file
# added there would be silently unversionable — `git add` would refuse it while
# `git status` stayed clean. The !*.go negation below cannot rescue that: git
# will not re-include a file inside an excluded directory.
/tool-store
/bin/

# Runtime data. The service's SQLite lives under ~/.config/tool-store/, but a
# stray dev copy in the tree should never be committed.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Byte-compiled Python from the sabotage scorers under scripts/. Every scorer
# run rewrites these, so without the rule the tree is dirty the moment anyone
# scores anything here — and a dirty tree is the signal an unattended pass reads
# as "another agent is working in this repo, leave it alone". An accidental
# artifact would be manufacturing the indicator we use to stay out of each
# other's way; skill-store committed one and paid exactly that cost.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Host-local config (machine-specific systemd drop-ins, dev secrets, etc.).
# Put anything that should never leave this machine under ./.local/
/.local/

# Defensive: never accidentally commit credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
credentials.*
secrets.*

# The globs above target secret *data* files, but they also match source
# (credentials.* once swallowed llm-bridge-server's internal/harness/credentials.go,
# leaving the committed tree unbuildable while `git status` stayed clean).
# Source is never a secret. Files under /.local/ stay ignored — git cannot
# re-include through an excluded directory.
!*.go
!*.sql
